WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.005 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
A human demonstration contains more than a goal.

2
00:00:03.005 --> 00:00:06.009 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
It shows a procedure: how to approach an object,

3
00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:08.576 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
coordinate movement, and complete a task.

4
00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:11.960 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
But a robot does not follow exactly the same path.

5
00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.321 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
It also needs to remember what actually

6
00:00:14.321 --> 00:00:16.379 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
happened during its own execution.

7
00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:20.547 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
The reference video builds a persistent demonstration-intent

8
00:00:20.547 --> 00:00:23.344 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
memory. Semantic and motion features capture

9
00:00:23.344 --> 00:00:26.141 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
what the procedure means and how it unfolds.

10
00:00:26.591 --> 00:00:28.746 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
A second memory tracks interaction

11
00:00:28.746 --> 00:00:31.408 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
progress using robot observations, states,

12
00:00:31.408 --> 00:00:34.197 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
and actions that have already been executed.

13
00:00:34.197 --> 00:00:37.493 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each action block reads intent first, then progress.

14
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:42.142 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
On Imitator Game, the Full50 checkpoint reaches eighty-four

15
00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:45.724 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
point six percent success across two thousand episodes.

16
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.041 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
We also evaluate RoboDemo on real household manipulation:

17
00:00:50.041 --> 00:00:53.291 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
organizing a tabletop, arranging sofa cushions,

18
00:00:53.291 --> 00:00:55.849 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
and pouring from a bottle into a cup.

19
00:00:56.299 --> 00:00:59.337 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
Across these three tasks, the model achieves a mean

20
00:00:59.337 --> 00:01:02.316 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
success rate of seventy-three point three percent.

21
00:01:02.316 --> 00:01:05.473 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here are excerpts from the recorded robot executions.

22
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.858 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
The same memory separation is useful when

23
00:01:08.858 --> 00:01:11.728 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
the environment changes. These recordings show

24
00:01:11.728 --> 00:01:14.535 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
tabletop organization under altered lighting,

25
00:01:14.535 --> 00:01:17.031 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
a different background, and a new scene.

26
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.620 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
When a human video is unavailable,

27
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:22.950 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
Refreward ranks robot demonstrations using the task

28
00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.018 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
instruction and the initial image. The selected

29
00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:29.283 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
procedure enters the same intent-memory interface.

30
00:01:29.633 --> 00:01:32.878 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
Explore the model architecture, five checkpoints,

31
00:01:32.878 --> 00:01:35.461 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
evaluation tools, and minimal examples.

32
00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:39.169 line:85% position:50% align:center size:90%
Learn the intent. Track the progress. Build on RoboDemo.
